 "skills": [
  {
   "id": "m3-24",
   "name": "Find and use the inverse of a 2 × 2 matrix"
  }
 ],
 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "The inverse A⁻¹ of a square matrix A satisfies AA⁻¹ = A⁻¹A = I.\nFor a 2 × 2 matrix: A⁻¹ = (1 ÷ |A|) × adj A. For A = (a b ; c d), A⁻¹ = 1/(ad − bc) × (d −b ; −c a).\n• If |A| = 0 (A singular), A has no inverse.\n• Check: AA⁻¹ = I.\n• Simultaneous equations ax + by = p, cx + dy = q can be written A(x ; y) = (p ; q), so (x ; y) = A⁻¹(p ; q).",
  "checks": []
 },
 "learn": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "sections": [
   {
    "heading": "Undoing a matrix",
    "text": "For numbers, {5} × {frac(1, 5)} = {1}: {frac(1, 5)} is the inverse of {5}. For matrices, the identity I plays the part of {1}.\nThe inverse of A is the matrix A⁻¹ with AA⁻¹ = A⁻¹A = I.\nFrom the last lesson, A × adj A = |A| × I. Divide by |A|: A⁻¹ = ({1} ÷ |A|) × adj A."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Finding it",
    "text": "A = {matStr([[5, 2], [7, 3]])}.\n• |A| = {15} − {14} = {1}.\n• adj A = {matStr([[3, -2], [-7, 5]])}.\n• A⁻¹ = ({1} ÷ {1}) × adj A = {matStr([[3, -2], [-7, 5]])}.\nIf |A| is, say, {2}, every element of the adjoint is divided by {2}. If |A| = {0}, you cannot divide: a singular matrix has no inverse."
   },
   {
    "heading": "Solving equations",
    "text": "{poly([5, 'x'], [2, 'y'])} = {16} and {poly([7, 'x'], [3, 'y'])} = {23} can be written A(x ; y) = ({16} ; {23}).\nMultiply both sides by A⁻¹: (x ; y) = A⁻¹({16} ; {23}).\nx = {3} × {16} + ({-2}) × {23} = {2}; y = ({-7}) × {16} + {5} × {23} = {3}.\nCheck: {5} × {2} + {2} × {3} = {16}. ✓"
   }
  ],
  "key_words": [
   {
    "word": "inverse matrix",
    "meaning": "A⁻¹, with AA⁻¹ = I"
   },
   {
    "word": "non-singular",
    "meaning": "determinant not {0}: the inverse exists"
   },
   {
    "word": "identity matrix",
    "meaning": "I = {matStr([[1, 0], [0, 1]])}"
   }
  ],
  "examples": [
   "{matStr([[2, 1], [1, 1]])}⁻¹ = {matStr([[1, -1], [-1, 2]])} (determinant {1})",
   "{matStr([[4, 2], [2, 1]])} has no inverse (determinant {0})"
  ],
  "mistake": {
   "wrong": "A⁻¹ = |A| × adj A",
   "right": "A⁻¹ = ({1} ÷ |A|) × adj A",
   "why": "You divide by the determinant. Check by multiplying: AA⁻¹ must give I."
  }
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {
   "A": [
    [
     5,
     2
    ],
    [
     7,
     3
    ]
   ]
  },
  "problem": "Find the inverse of A in the figure.",
  "steps": [
   "|A| = {A[0][0]} × {A[1][1]} − {A[0][1]} × {A[1][0]} = {A[0][0] * A[1][1]} − {A[0][1] * A[1][0]} = {det2(A)}.",
   "adj A = {matStr(adj2(A))}.",
   "A⁻¹ = ({1} ÷ {det2(A)}) × adj A = {matStr(adj2(A))}.",
   "Check: A × A⁻¹ = {matStr(matMul(A, adj2(A)))} = I. ✓"
  ],
  "answer": "A⁻¹ = {matStr(adj2(A))}",
  "checks": [
   "det2(A) == 1"
  ],
  "figure": "matFig([['A', A]])"
 },
